  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e1",
      "title": "Accent marks",
      "body": "Accents are part of the spelling. Some change the sound. Some only change the spelling. You must write them correctly, because a and à are different words, and ou and où are different words."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "t1",
      "title": "The accents",
      "headers": [
        "Mark",
        "On",
        "What it does",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "é (acute)",
          "é",
          "sound ay",
          "été (summer): ay-TAY"
        ],
        [
          "è, ê (grave, circumflex)",
          "è ê",
          "sound eh",
          "père (father): pehR · fête (party): feht"
        ],
        [
          "ë",
          "ë",
          "say the e separately",
          "Noël: noh-EL"
        ],
        [
          "à, â",
          "à â",
          "sound ah (no change)",
          "là (there): lah · âge (age): ahzh"
        ],
        [
          "ù, û",
          "ù û",
          "sound ü or oo, no change",
          "où (where): oo · sûr (sure): sür"
        ],
        [
          "ô",
          "ô",
          "sound oh",
          "hôtel: oh-TEL"
        ],
        [
          "î, ï",
          "î ï",
          "sound ee",
          "île (island): eel · maïs (corn): mah-EES"
        ],
        [
          "ç (cedilla)",
          "ç",
          "c sounds like s",
          "garçon (boy): gahR-SOH(N) · ça: sah"
        ],
        [
          "œ",
          "œ",
          "sound uh",
          "sœur (sister): suhR · œuf (egg): uhf"
        ]
      ],
      "hear": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e2",
      "title": "Watch out",
      "body": "é and è are two different sounds. été is ay-TAY. mère is mehR. a (has) and à (to, at) are different words. ou (or) and où (where) are different words."
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e3",
      "title": "In Canada",
      "body": "Accents are everywhere in Canadian names: Montréal, Québec, Trois-Rivières, Gaspésie, rue Sainte-Catherine. In French, capital letters keep their accents: À, É."
    },
    {
